course: dictionary
lesson: 16168
title: Wrecked: damaged, ruined, or very tired
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wrecked has more than one meaning, so context matters. «The wrecked ship lay on the sea floor for a hundred years.» A ship on the sea floor is badly damaged, so here wrecked means badly damaged or destroyed.
explain: Look at the words after it. «The rain wrecked our picnic plans.» The plans were not broken like a boat, but they were spoilt and ruined. Wrecked can mean spoilt or ruined when we talk about plans or days.
explain: «After the football match, Sam said, "I'm wrecked!" and flopped onto the sofa.» Sam is not damaged. The flop onto the sofa is the clue: wrecked here means very tired.
explain: Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. A wrecked car is not a tired car, so the clues around the word tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Wrecked means badly damaged or destroyed, like a wrecked car or a wrecked ship.
fact: A sailor whose ship is wrecked is shipwrecked.
fact: Wrecked plans or days are spoilt or ruined.
fact: In everyday talk, especially in the UK and Australia, «I'm wrecked» means I am very tired.
fact: Wrecked is also the past form of the verb wreck: «The storm wrecked the old boat last night.»
exercise: «The wrecked ship lay on the sea floor for a hundred years.» What does wrecked mean here? | Brand new and shiny | Very tired after a long swim | Happy to be at sea | *Badly damaged or destroyed
exercise: «The storm wrecked our picnic plans.» What does wrecked mean in this sentence? | Made a little bit bigger | Cooked very slowly | *Spoilt or ruined | Finished on time
exercise: «"I'm wrecked after the match," said Priya, and she sat down.» What does wrecked mean? | Very rich | *Very tired | Very quiet | Very wet from the rain
test: «The old car was wrecked in the crash.» Which word could you swap in for wrecked without changing the meaning? | Cleaned | Painted | Parked | *Damaged
test: Which sentence uses wrecked to mean very tired? | The wrecked house was painted blue. | The wrecked ship sank near the rocks. | *We were wrecked after our long hike up the hill. | The wrecked bridge was closed to cars.
exam: Ella says, «I'm wrecked, I need a nap!» What does Ella mean? | She has broken something important | *She is very tired | She is lost at sea | She is very happy to be awake
